      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/43/848",
      "text": [
        " اَلصَّلاَةِ ثُمَّ يَنْظُرُ بَعْدَ مَا فَرَغَ فَيَرَى أَنَّهُ قَدِ اِنْحَرَفَ عَنِ اَلْقِبْلَةِ يَمِيناً أَوْ شِمَالاً فَقَالَ لَهُ «قَدْ مَضَتْ صَلاَتُهُ وَ مَا بَيْنَ اَلْمَشْرِقِ وَ اَلْمَغْرِبِ قِبْلَةٌ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.848 - Muawiya ibn Ammar asked Him about a man who stands for prayer and, after finishing, realizes that he had deviated to the right or the left of the Qiblah.\nImam (as) replied: \"His prayer is valid, for the area between the east and the west is (considered) the Qiblah.\""
        ]
      }
